aluable for long-distance flights. However, C is unfriendly and eats unhealthily, which may affect crew cooperation. Compared to B, C's strengths in situational awareness may outweigh B's interpersonal issues, but we need to weigh the unfriendly attitude. I think we should evaluate C as a strong alternative.\"\n\nWe need to state our current recommendation. Could be still B, but we are opening discussion. We could say we still lean towards B but want to consider C. Or we could shift to C. The guidelines: we must state a current recommendation. So we can say \"My provisional recommendation remains Candidate B, but I think we should also examine Candidate C as a strong alternative.\" That satisfies.\n\nThus metadata vote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce output."}
